          "distinct": true,
          "id": "ffc3e36442259b7171936cea580f855820de4804",
          "message": "feat(sparq-trust): opt-in property-admissibility pre-check in the admission gate (sq-dt5hv) [OPUS-4.8] (#1230)\n\nPhase 5 of the security-properties ontology epic (sq-0dksu): add ONE optional\npre-admission check to the trust-graph PoC admission gate, behind a new default-OFF\n`secprop-precheck` cargo feature. Before the existing signature / freshness / holder\nchecks, consult the merged secprop reduction (Phase 2 `admissible`, over the Phase 3\nper-method annotation graph + the Phase 4 ODRL leftOperands) to decide whether the\nPRESENTED proof method satisfies the requester's machine-reasonable ODRL privacy\npreference — and DENY fail-closed (default-deny) on non-satisfaction.\n\nWHAT:\n- crates/sparq-trust/src/admit.rs — a feature-gated `precheck` module:\n  `admit_with_precheck(cred, rules, session, target, preference)`,\n  `AdmissibilityPreference { method_iri, constraint_iris, policy_n3, annotations_n3 }`,\n  and `PrecheckOutcome { Admitted, Denied { unsatisfied }, ReductionError { error } }`.\n  It is a THIN DRIVER over the merged `admissibility::admissible` reduction — it does\n  NOT redefine it. 7 unit tests + the e2e suite below.\n- crates/sparq-trust/tests/secprop_precheck_e2e.rs — the golden integration suite over\n  the REAL admit path (RDFC-1.0 commit + CHECKED issuer Schnorr signature + SHACL\n  scoping + clear-WebID holder binding): the load-bearing invariants are byte-identical\n  `None` path, satisfied-preference admits + derives the age>18 grant, and an\n  unsatisfied `requiresAssurance gteq Proven` FAILS CLOSED (admits nothing, derives no\n  grant) despite a perfectly valid credential — the principled refusal, in the data flow.\n- Cargo.toml — the default-OFF `secprop-precheck` feature (enables\n  `secprop-admissibility`); NO new dependency.\n- lib.rs — re-export the precheck surface behind the feature (doc-cfg gated).\n- .github/feature-matrix.d/sparq-trust.yml + scripts/tests/feature-matrix-legnames.golden.txt\n  — a new gating leg `opt-in sparq-trust (secprop-precheck — …)` so the otherwise\n  silently-skipped cfg-gated tests run on CI (the assemble + golden tests pass).\n- README + skills/access-control/SKILL.md — document the pre-check, its opt-in\n  byte-identical-with-None semantics, the fail-closed boundary, and the honest scope.\n\nHONEST BOUNDARY: it reasons over recorded ANNOTATIONS, not cryptography; the verdict is\nonly as honest as the annotation graph. sparq's whole ZK estate is research-grade and\nexternally UNAUDITED (sq-qhy4 — external accredited-cryptographer sign-off PENDING);\nsparq-mpc is semi-honest-only. `requiresAssurance gteq secx:Proven` mechanically removes\nevery sparq ZK method today. The pre-check can only ever DENY, never broaden, and never\nweakens a downstream crypto check. STRICT ADDITIVITY: with no preference the gate is\nbyte-identical to `admit`; the lean default build is unchanged with the feature OFF.\n\nGates GREEN both feature states (default OFF + secprop-precheck ON, incl --all-features):\ncargo build/test/clippy --all-targets -D warnings; rustdoc --workspace --no-deps\n--all-features RUSTDOCFLAGS=-D warnings clean; check-privacy-claims OK; readme-template 0\ndeviations (README ≤120); feature-matrix assemble + golden tests pass. NO new dependency.\n\n🤖 SPARQ agent — trust-graph authorisation PoC / security-properties ontology. Written\nwhile Fable unavailable — flag for re-review when Fable returns.\n\nCo-authored-by: Jesse Wright <jmwright.045@gmail.com>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>",
          "timestamp": "2026-06-23T07:55:58Z",
